<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.842 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.842 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.6 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due May 15, 1997 was 2.842 percent, down from 2.864 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 182-day T-bills due August 14, 1997 was 3.133 percent, down from 3.162 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due February 5, 1998 was 3.444 percent, down from 3.567 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$175 million six-month and C$50 million one-year bills. It holds C$800 million of C$5.2 billion bills due Feb. 20.</p>
